sam (docs): created a tiny docs PR: short cookbook for tool-calling + structured output. goal: one small example, migration note, and parse fallback. please eyeball.
ivy (eng): quick ask: include both py + ts snippets? most teams copy one or the other.
sam (docs): yes both. very compact. show request, expected JSON schema, and a safe fallback.
omar (eng-ml): add a nullable field example to show how to accept missing results. schema idea: {
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "id": {"type": "string"},
    "answer": {"anyOf": [{"type": "null"}, {"type": "object"}] }
  },
  "required": ["id"]
}

sam (docs): nice. ivy: can you paste the TS parse+fallback snippet (2 lines)?
ivy (eng): pasted: const r = await client.tools.call('analyze', input); const payload = tryParse(r.output) ?? {error: 'parse_failed'};
